.el .ds Aq '
.TH marquee-markdown 1  "marquee-markdown 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
marquee\-markdown \- A TUI markdown reader that renders documents like Claude artifacts, with a table\-of\-contents panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmarquee\-markdown\fR [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-line\-numbers\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-pager\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-preserve\-new\-lines\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-style\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-tui\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fISOURCE\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A TUI markdown reader that renders documents like Claude artifacts, with a table\-of\-contents panel
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR
Show hidden and git\-ignored files when browsing
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-line\-numbers\fR
Show line numbers
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mouse\fR
Enable mouse wheel scrolling
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-pager\fR
Display with a pager
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-preserve\-new\-lines\fR
Preserve newlines within paragraphs
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-style\fR \fI<STYLE>\fR
Style name, or a path to a theme file.

No clap default: an unset flag has to stay unset so it does not override a configuration file. The default lives in the defaults layer, with every other default.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tui\fR
Display in the full\-screen reader
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR
Word\-wrap width; 0 disables wrapping
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to a configuration file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fISOURCE\fR]
File, directory, URL, or `owner/repo` shorthand. `\-` reads stdin
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
marquee\-markdown\-themes(1)
List the available styles and where they came from
.TP
marquee\-markdown\-config(1)
Print the configuration in force, as a file that would produce it
.TP
marquee\-markdown\-keys(1)
Print the key bindings as markdown
.TP
marquee\-markdown\-man(1)
Print a man page to standard output
.TP
marquee\-markdown\-completion(1)
Print a shell completion script to standard output
.TP
marquee\-markdown\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
